<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>

A powerful unarmed strike using your legs. The kick command
automatically adapts to the combat situation:

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Kick (standing target) ━━━</ansi>

  A solid kick with a chance to knock the target prone.
  Good damage and the knockdown opens up follow-up stomps.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Stomp (prone target) ━━━</ansi>

  When the target is already on the ground, your kick becomes
  a devastating stomp that bypasses half their armor. Also
  extends how long they stay down. This is the payoff for
  knocking someone prone.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Knee (grapple, in control) ━━━</ansi>

  When you have control in a clinch or ground grapple, your
  kick becomes a close-range knee strike. Strong damage that
  works where kicks can't.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>       Auto-selects variant based on position.
  <ansi fg="command">stomp</ansi>      Alias for kick (stomps if target is prone).
  <ansi fg="command">knee</ansi>       Alias for kick (knees if in grapple control).

Requires being in combat. Shares a cooldown with other
special moves (bash, trip). Uses the <ansi fg="skill">unarmed-combat</ansi> skill.

<ansi fg="magenta-bold">See also:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">help bash</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help trip</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help grapple</ansi>
